# Anywhere, not just the root. `tests/Browser/widget` has a package.json of
# its own (the Playwright harness), and a rooted pattern leaves its
# node_modules untracked-but-not-ignored — so the next `git add -A` stages a
# few thousand files nobody meant to commit.
#
# No trailing slash on purpose: with one, the pattern matches directories only,
# and on this machine that path is a symlink — which git then happily staged as
# a single file.
node_modules

# The compiled CSS and JS are committed on purpose. Shared hosting has no Node,
# and a deploy that needs `npm run build` is a deploy that fails with a white
# page (docs/DEPLOY.md). Run the build locally and commit what changes.
# /public/build
